[19:29:53] ✓   --- CONCLUSION ---
[19:29:53] ✓   On real INPOP19a residuals, the central synodic carrier survives at 59.6% after an 82-parameter basis fit, while the mean sideband survival is 90.9%. For the synthetic dynamically modulated TEP signal, carrier survival is 58.7% and sideband mean survival is 90.7%. The sidebands (D±M, D±annual) are substantially more robust to absorption than the central carrier in this linear stress test. This spectral persistence is evidence that the residual signal carries a dynamical sideband signature. This proxy is a linear regression stress test, not a symplectic N-body integrator, and cannot emulate the iterative dynamic potentials of the actual Fortran/C++ code underlying INPOP or DE430. The definitive external confirmation remains a source-level INPOP/DE430 refit with η or the equivalent TEP parameter explicitly estimated.
